# ESP-PredictiveMesh - Stage 1 sdkconfig defaults
#
# Minimal overrides for an ESP-NOW point-to-point test:
# - Default single-app partition table is sufficient.
# - Static/Dynamic allocation buffers left at IDF defaults (no extra heap needed).
# - Keep Wi-Fi country code permissive for international 2.4 GHz use.
# - Disable power save so ESP-NOW transmissions are not delayed.

# Use the default partition table shipped with ESP-IDF (single app).
# (No custom partition overrides required for Stage 1.)

# Allow operation on channels 1-13 without a real AP connection
CONFIG_WIFI_COUNTRY_CODE="01"

# Disable modem sleep to keep ESP-NOW packet timing consistent.
# (Stage 1 uses a 1 Hz send cadence; power save is irrelevant here.)
# ESP-NOW itself does not require disabling power save, but we leave it
# off for predictable Stage 1 behaviour. Revisit in later stages.

# Default to the IDF-default Wi-Fi country policy (auto).
